  '{"folder":"essays","category":"工作流","tags":["workflow","notes"],"reading_time":4,"template_id":"page_tpl_article"}', 'ver_art_garden_1', 'admin', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, '2026-11-18 09:30:00'
);
INSERT INTO entity_versions (id, site_id, entity_type, entity_id, version_number, title, summary, content_raw, metadata_snapshot, commit_message, author_id) VALUES ('ver_art_garden_1', 'site_default', 'article', 'art_digital_garden', 1, '构建我的数字花园工作流', '从灵感捕捉、知识双链到中英双语同步的轻量发布日常。', '建立一套低摩擦的写作与创作工作流，关键不在于工具多复杂，而在于随时打开就能把想法写下来，并让它们自然生长成有序的知识网。

[[tip: 相关前篇：回到 [[hello-walnut|你好，数字花园]] 了解本站的内容组织原则。]]

## 1. 从碎片输入到常青笔记

日常看到有意思的思路时，我习惯先发一条简短动态或记录在草稿里，周末再把同类零散想法合并整理成一篇可读的长文。

### 双向链接的价值

当你在一篇新随笔中顺手提及旧文章时，右侧栏会自动出现双向关联记录，让久未翻开的思考重新串联起来。

## 2. 保持双语同步的节奏

写完中文版后，只需把核心观点提炼翻译成自然地道的目标语言版本，就能让同一套排版与项目展示同时服务更多读者。', '{}', 'Initial ZH workflow essay', 'admin');

INSERT INTO articles (id, site_id, slug, locale, translation_group_id, status, visibility, maturity, title, summary, cover_image_url, metadata, current_version_id, curator_id, published_at, created_at) VALUES (
  'art_digital_garden_en', 'site_default', 'building-digital-garden', 'en-US', 'tg_art_2', 'published', 'public', 'evergreen', 'Building a Bilingual Digital Garden Workflow', 'From quick sparks and wiki backlinks to maintaining aligned Chinese and English essays.', '',
  '{"folder":"essays","category":"Workflow","tags":["workflow","notes"],"reading_time":4,"template_id":"page_tpl_article"}', 'ver_art_garden_en_1', 'admin', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, '2026-11-18 09:25:00'
);
INSERT INTO entity_versions (id, site_id, entity_type, entity_id, version_number, title, summary, content_raw, metadata_snapshot, commit_message, author_id) VALUES ('ver_art_garden_en_1', 'site_default', 'article', 'art_digital_garden_en', 1, 'Building a Bilingual Digital Garden Workflow', 'From quick sparks and wiki backlinks to maintaining aligned Chinese and English essays.', 'A low-friction publishing routine matters far more than an elaborate setup. The goal is simply to capture ideas quickly and let useful patterns emerge over time.

[[tip: Companion essay: revisit [[hello-walnut|Hello, Digital Garden]] for the overall content philosophy.]]

## 1. From Quick Sparks to Evergreen Essays

Small thoughts begin as short stream entries during the week, then gradually coalesce into structured essays whenever a theme repeats itself.

### Why Backlinks Matter

Linking related notes creates quiet serendipity across topics—revisiting one essay surfaces connected ideas without maintaining rigid folder trees.

## 2. Writing Naturally in Two Languages

Keeping paired Chinese and English versions lets essays, templates, and navigation stay aligned without sacrificing natural phrasing in either language.', '{}', 'Initial EN workflow essay', 'admin');

